    "Gibran Rakabuming Raka has formally departed the Vice Presidential Palace following his resignation.",
    "President Prabowo Subianto is currently coordinating with coalition parties to identify two potential candidates for the vacancy.",
    "Parliamentary leaders have expressed an expectation for an orderly transition process targeted for completion by late November."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the official resignation of Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka, the Indonesian government has entered a period of transition to fill the vacancy. Gibran Rakabuming Raka has concluded his duties at the Vice Presidential Palace and held farewell meetings with staff and supporters. In response, President Prabowo Subianto is reportedly preparing to consult with members of his governing coalition to finalize a list of two candidates for the position. Members of the House of Representatives, specifically from Commission III, have held discussions with the President regarding the constitutional procedures required for the appointment of a new Vice President. Law experts and parliamentary figures noted that the selection process involves collaborative dialogue between the executive branch and allied political parties. Official projections from legislative representatives indicate that the transition process is intended to conclude by November 26, 2026, ensuring administrative continuity within the Indonesian government.",
